    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      243.25,
      401.92,
      266.56
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      279.85,
      401.88,
      303.16
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Judicature (Amendment)Act, No. of 2017.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      316.45,
      401.86,
      352.0
    ],
    "text": "2.Section 4 of the Judicature Act, No. 2 of 1978 is herebyamended by the repeal of paragraph (a) of that section andthe substitution therefor of the following paragraph:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.77,
      365.29,
      401.89,
      400.72
    ],
    "text": "\u201c(a) not less than ten and not more than eighty five judges,each of whom shall be known as a \u201cJudge of theHigh Court;\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      414.25,
      401.89,
      437.56
    ],
    "text": "3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
